      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-223545",
      ":question/problem": "The number of hours of daylight in Oslo, Norway, can be modeled by a function of the form\n$T(t) = 6.5\\cos (\\frac{\u03c0t}{182}) + 12$,\nwhere $t$ is the time (in days). How many hours of daylight was there in Oslo on March 20, when the hours of daylight is midway between its maximum and minimum value?"
